#
# Rakuten Viber (iOS) 29.4 Zero-Size Logical Screen GIF Remote 1-Tap Crash
#
#
# Vendor: Viber Media S.a.r.l.
# Product web page: https://www.viber.com
# Affected version: 29.4.0.24, 29.3, 29.2.2, 29.1.2
#
# Summary: Viber is a calling and messaging app that connects
# people - no matter who they are, or where they’re from. Each
# month, hundreds of millions of people connect, for free, with
# their loved ones via messaging, high-quality voice and video
# calls, and more. All one-on-one Viber calls and personal chats,
# and all group chats are protected by built-in end-to-end encryption,
# so you can be sure that your conversations are always secure.
#
# Desc: Viber for iOS doesn't validate the logical screen dimensions
# in the header of a received GIF. When the user opens the GIF,
# Viber builds a placeholder image sized from those dimensions by
# calling +[UIImage(Utils) imageWithColor:size:opaque:] (in ViberCoreUILegacy),
# which calls UIKit’s UIGraphicsBeginImageContextWithOptions. If
# the width or the height is zero, UIKit can't create the bitmap
# and raises an NSInternalInconsistencyException. Viber doesn't
# catch it, so the app aborts with SIGABRT on the main thread. Viber's
# servers relay the GIF unchanged, so any user can deliver it to
# any other user. Every GIF with a zero-width or zero-height canvas
# tested this way crashed, static and animated alike.
#
